arison for icanhazstring. It gives only per-directory shares (6% and 16%) and no overall 11.7%. It does show Carlos and Kévin as having left. The missing comparison fails the criterion.\", \"pass\": false}], \"C\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer C reports Ben at 62.6% overall on non-blank lines and 60.9% with blanks, inside the 55-63% range. Its src/ figure of 70.1% (non-blank) is in range, and tests/ at 55.2% (non-blank) is in range. Ben is named the largest owner with his addresses merged.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer C does not credit Grouping to Katarzyna Nowak. It lists Grouping among files nobody remaining knows, and its tables leave Nowak out entirely despite listing contributors down to 0.5%. In its view the lines still belong to Ben or to no one, so it fails.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Tomasz Wrona is at 1.8-1.9%, or 1.5% after ignoring the mechanical commits. Both the rename and the php-cs-fixer commit are treated as non-authorship, and the generated TypeMap and the bot are left out. Nothing credits src/Support to Tomasz.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer C gives a bus factor of 1 and 62.6% of lines lost if Ben left (in range for ~59%). It says the others last committed in 2019 or earlier. However, it says 35.4% belong to people who left, and 64.6% sit with 3 'active' people. That is the opposite of the ~96% with no active author. It also misses Katarzyna's active status. The 90-98% figure fails.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer C gives icanhazstring 11.3-11.7% of lines against a lower commit share, and notes Carlos has 15.5% of commits but 7% of lines. It lists last commits of 2016 (Carlos) and 2018 (Kévin), so both are shown as having left. Bots are excluded. The commit-versus-line contrast is shown, though not for icanhazstring specifically. Overall the criterion is satisfied.\", \"pass\": true}]}","ttft_ms":12726,"type":"result","duration_ms":12752,"uuid":"d3465bee-f810-4